Performing this substitution, we have:

f(2) = 4(2)^3 - 9(2) - 14.

This means we take 2 and raise it to the power of 3, which is the same as cubing 2. After obtaining the result of 2 cubed, we multiply this result by 4. Simultaneously, we also multiply 9 by 2 and then subtract both 9 times 2 and 14 from the product of 4 and the cube of 2. 

