In this solution, we first check if the lengths of the two arrays are equal. If they are, we can simply take the median of the two arrays by averaging the elements at the middle position. This means that we calculate the median by taking the middle elements of both arrays, adding them together, and then dividing by two. By doing this, we effectively find the point that lies in the center of both arrays when they are of equal length.

